.\" Manpage for system-update
.TH SYSTEM-UPDATE 1 "2026" "awesome-updater 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
system-update \- Manjaro unattended system updater
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B system-update
.RI [ OPTION ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B system-update
is the main executable provided by the
.B awesome-updater
package.
It performs an unattended Manjaro system update, tracks kernel package
changes, and schedules a one-time system reboot if required.
.PP
The command is intended to be run from the user's crontab. It is also safe
to run interactively.
.PP
A complete default configuration is installed by the package at
.IR /etc/system-update/config.conf .
No manual setup is required for typical use.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show a short usage message and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version of
.B system-update
and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-status
Print the current state (running kernel, pending reboot, attention
required) without performing any update. Read-only.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration is loaded from the following sources. Later sources override
earlier ones:
.IP "1." 4
Built-in defaults compiled into
.BR system-update .
.IP "2." 4
.IR /etc/system-update/config.conf
installed by the package.
.IP "3." 4
.IR ~/.config/system-update/config.conf
optional per-user overrides.
.PP
The configuration format is plain
.IR KEY=VALUE .
No shell code is executed.
Unknown keys are ignored.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/system-update/config.conf
System-wide configuration installed by the package.
.TP
.I ~/.config/system-update/config.conf
Optional per-user overrides.
.TP
.I /var/lib/system-update/attention.state
Current attention state written by the updater.
.TP
.I /var/lib/system-update/kernel-reboot-needed
Persistent kernel reboot state written by the updater.
.TP
.I ~/logs/latest_update.log
Symlink to the most recent update log.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR system-update-notify (1),
.BR pacman (8),
.BR systemd-run (1),
.BR crontab (5)
